## Example Usage

```hcl
data "axual_group" "team-bonanza" {
  name = "Team Bonanza"
}

resource "axual_topic" "logs" {
  name = "logs"
  key_type = "String"
  value_type = "String"
  owners = data.axual_group.team-bonanza.id
  retention_policy = "delete"
  properties = { propertyKey1: "propertyValue1", propertyKey2: "propertyValue2"}
  description = "Logs from all applications"
  tags = ["logging", "platform"]
}

resource "axual_topic" "example_avro" {
  name = "example_avro_topic"
  key_type = "AVRO"
  key_schema = axual_schema_version.axual_gitops_test_schema_version1.schema_id
  value_type = "AVRO"
  value_schema = axual_schema_version.axual_gitops_test_schema_version2.schema_id
  owners = data.axual_group.team-bonanza.id
  retention_policy = "delete"
  properties = { }
  description = "Logs from all applications with Avro schema"
}
```

The schema versions `axual_gitops_test_schema_version1` and `axual_gitops_test_schema_version2` are defined in the `axual_schema_version` example.

For a full example which shows the capabilities of the latest Terraform provider, check https://github.com/Axual/terraform-provider-axual/tree/master/examples/axual.

## Import

Import is supported by ID, or by name (`name:`):

```shell
terraform import axual_topic.<LOCAL NAME> <TOPIC UID>
terraform import axual_topic.test_topic b21cf1d63a55436391463cee3f56e393
terraform import axual_topic.<LOCAL NAME> name:<TOPIC NAME>
terraform import axual_topic.test_topic 'name:payments'
```

The name must match exactly, case included. An `import` block (Terraform 1.5 or later) takes the same IDs:

```terraform
import {
  to = axual_topic.test_topic
  id = "name:payments"
}
```

In Terraform 1.12 or later, an `import` block can use `identity` instead of `id`:

```terraform
import {
  to = axual_topic.example
  identity = {
    id = "b21cf1d63a55436391463cee3f56e393"
  }
}
```

